From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:58:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: a swapchain's last Release frees it

MTLD3D12SwapChain is a DXGI object (ComObjectWithInitialRef: it starts
with one reference), but CreateSwapChain wrapped it in Com(new ...),
which added another, so after the caller's last Release one reference
was left: the swapchain, its back buffers and its metal view were never
freed. In the game VM the view stayed over the window when its game
ended (3DMark's Steel Nomad's last frame hid 3DMark's UI). Com::transfer
adopts the initial reference instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp b/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp
index 4170912..4ca8bc2 100644
--- a/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp
@@ -983,7 +983,10 @@ CreateSwapChain(
     const DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_DESC1 *pDesc, const DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_FULLSCREEN_DESC *pFullscreenDesc,
     IDXGISwapChain1 **ppSwapChain
 ) {
-  auto swapchain = Com(new MTLD3D12SwapChain(pFactory, pDevice, pQueue, hWnd, pDesc, pFullscreenDesc));
+  // A DXGI object starts with its reference (ComObjectWithInitialRef): adopted, not added to, or the swapchain and its
+  // view outlive the last Release.
+  auto swapchain =
+      Com<MTLD3D12SwapChain>::transfer(new MTLD3D12SwapChain(pFactory, pDevice, pQueue, hWnd, pDesc, pFullscreenDesc));
   HRESULT hr = swapchain->ResizeBuffers(0, pDesc->Width, pDesc->Height, DXGI_FORMAT_UNKNOWN, 0);
   if (FAILED(hr))
     return hr;
